Silo-only: out-of-range raw/structured buffer loads return 0 and out-of-range stores are dropped, as D3D defines.

Why: God of War (2018) with AMD FSR 2 on was far darker than with FSR off or on GPTK, darker the lower the FSR
mode. Measured on device (2026-10-19) with read-back probes: the game's auto-exposure is a GPU reduction
(`luminancePartAio`) over a 240x135 luminance image that it reads back as a 16-byte buffer. With FSR on, the
game sizes the intermediate partial-sum buffer from the reduced render resolution (816 B = 51 elements) but
still dispatches 4x135 groups into it. On D3D that is harmless — the excess stores are dropped, the excess
loads read 0 and the final ratio sum(x)/sum(z) ignores them. airconv instead pointed an out-of-range access
at a null address, which on Metal neither drops the store nor reads 0: the reduction picked up garbage
(positive values where a negative log-luminance belongs) and the exposure came out ~6.6 EV low (-0.91 instead
of ~5.8). With this patch the reduction gives the FSR-off value and the picture matches GPTK.

The null-address select is kept so the access itself still never leaves the buffer; the value / the store is
now also guarded explicitly. Shader cache version bumped so converted shaders are not reused.

Not upstream. Rebase onto each DXMT_VERSION bump.

